1
00:00:15,660 --> 00:00:24,720
Q: Can you describe the Four Noble Truths

2
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:28,980
that the Buddha teaches? Suffering, is

3
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:32,490
the First Noble Truth, there is suffering, second,

4
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:36,150
there is the cause of suffering. 3rd, cessation of

5
00:00:36,150 --> 00:00:41,100
suffering and 4th, Path leading to the cessation of suffering.

6
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:44,580
A: Well, first and foremost,

7
00:00:44,580 --> 00:00:47,700
they are 4 descriptions, or

8
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:53,470
four aspects of one insight, that insight being freedom

9
00:00:53,470 --> 00:00:57,280
from suffering basically, feel free from suffering,

10
00:00:57,780 --> 00:00:58,370
that already implies

11
00:00:58,370 --> 00:01:00,080
the knowledge of what suffering is,

12
00:01:00,080 --> 00:01:01,960
that already implies

13
00:01:01,960 --> 00:01:04,140
the knowledge of what has been causing

14
00:01:04,140 --> 00:01:07,680
that suffering, that already implies the knowledge of freedom from suffering

15
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:11,390
and that already implies the knowledge of how to maintain, that freedom from suffering,

16
00:01:11,390 --> 00:01:16,030
that insight.

17
00:01:16,030 --> 00:01:16,710
Q: How to develop it?

18
00:01:16,710 --> 00:01:20,660
A: well, how to maintain, which basically then

19
00:01:20,660 --> 00:01:22,580
results in complete Liberation

20
00:01:22,580 --> 00:01:31,490
from all the Upakkilesa and all the other kinds of pollution.

21
00:01:31,490 --> 00:01:35,690
So it's not like 1, 2, 3, 4 that the person needs to discern

22
00:01:35,690 --> 00:01:36,400
one by one,

23
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:41,910
basically, suffering and freedom from it.

24
00:01:41,910 --> 00:01:44,750
And that's what many suttas mention

25
00:01:44,750 --> 00:01:47,070
basically. It would only

26
00:01:47,070 --> 00:01:51,170
talk about the cause of suffering.

27
00:01:51,170 --> 00:01:56,810
Cause of suffering is, Nothing else except Craving

28
00:01:56,810 --> 00:01:58,590
and that's again,

29
00:01:58,590 --> 00:02:04,730
that's something that people might read over, and it seems like

30
00:02:04,730 --> 00:02:06,050
it's making sense

31
00:02:06,050 --> 00:02:06,430
of course

32
00:02:06,430 --> 00:02:09,720
But actually, in terms of the direct insight,

33
00:02:09,720 --> 00:02:11,680
seeing the craving is suffering

34
00:02:11,680 --> 00:02:13,670
results in Liberation from that suffering

35
00:02:13,670 --> 00:02:15,960
Seeing

36
00:02:15,960 --> 00:02:16,770
the craving, means

37
00:02:16,770 --> 00:02:19,650
abandoning the craving, so the only reason you crave, is

38
00:02:19,650 --> 00:02:21,060
you don't really see it,

39
00:02:21,060 --> 00:02:22,410
directly you don't understand it,

40
00:02:22,410 --> 00:02:26,150
you haven't discerned it.

41
00:02:26,150 --> 00:02:28,090
And

42
00:02:28,090 --> 00:02:30,000
important aspect is to recognize that

43
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:32,770
whenever there is suffering present,

44
00:02:32,770 --> 00:02:35,710
you can

45
00:02:35,710 --> 00:02:38,940
induce correctly,

46
00:02:38,940 --> 00:02:40,570
that the craving must be present

47
00:02:40,570 --> 00:02:43,740
because suffering is there.

48
00:02:43,740 --> 00:02:48,780
So it's not like, ''oh I suffer, now I have to look for the reason'', call it

49
00:02:48,780 --> 00:02:52,540
craving or something else or also assuming that sometimes, something else

50
00:02:52,540 --> 00:02:52,870
can be

51
00:02:52,870 --> 00:02:55,260
the cause of your suffering.

52
00:02:55,260 --> 00:02:57,070
Really needs to be brought down so narrowly

53
00:02:57,070 --> 00:02:59,010
and so precisely

54
00:02:59,010 --> 00:03:02,110
whereby you discern when the suffering,

55
00:03:02,110 --> 00:03:02,800
the disagreeable

56
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:04,740
unpleasant feeling that you are resisting

57
00:03:04,740 --> 00:03:06,660
basically, when the suffering is present,

58
00:03:06,660 --> 00:03:07,440
means, it's because

59
00:03:07,440 --> 00:03:11,480
simultaneously with it, there is craving present.

60
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:13,950
The absence of the craving, simultaneously means

61
00:03:13,950 --> 00:03:15,260
the absence of that suffering,

62
00:03:15,260 --> 00:03:16,960
there is no delay.

63
00:03:16,960 --> 00:03:17,330
That's why

64
00:03:17,330 --> 00:03:20,010
you can have the direct knowledge of freedom

65
00:03:20,010 --> 00:03:23,710
from suffering, directly verified for yourself.

66
00:03:23,710 --> 00:03:27,190
You cannot suffer amid suffering as the Buddha

67
00:03:27,190 --> 00:03:28,430
would often say,

68
00:03:28,430 --> 00:03:31,840
literally amid the things that used to make you suffer,

69
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:34,130
the mind cannot suffer now

70
00:03:34,130 --> 00:03:36,480
because there is no more craving in regard to those

71
00:03:36,480 --> 00:03:40,770
things.

72
00:03:40,770 --> 00:03:41,820
Q: How to abandon craving?

73
00:03:41,820 --> 00:03:48,810
A: How to abandon craving? Well, sense restraint,

74
00:03:48,810 --> 00:03:53,860
Virtue, developed to the extent necessary, whereby you start

75
00:03:53,860 --> 00:03:56,750
discerning then, your mental intentions,

76
00:03:56,750 --> 00:03:59,140
whether they're rooted in wholesome

77
00:03:59,140 --> 00:04:01,380
unwholesome, whether they're rooted in greed

78
00:04:01,380 --> 00:04:02,480
aversion, delusion.

79
00:04:02,480 --> 00:04:03,810
And when you know that they are,

80
00:04:03,810 --> 00:04:06,740
you do not engage in them, you do not tolerate them, you do not

81
00:04:06,740 --> 00:04:07,680
entertain them, you do not

82
00:04:07,680 --> 00:04:09,760
proliferate them, you do not invest

83
00:04:09,760 --> 00:04:11,590
in them.

84
00:04:11,590 --> 00:04:14,040
That would basically enable the mind to then

85
00:04:14,040 --> 00:04:16,530
Not resist the unpleasant

86
00:04:16,530 --> 00:04:19,910
feeling, to Not indulge the pleasant

87
00:04:19,910 --> 00:04:22,940
feeling, to Not try to distract yourself

88
00:04:22,940 --> 00:04:26,320
from neutral feeling. And when mind stops doing

89
00:04:26,320 --> 00:04:28,840
that, with the previous knowledge

90
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:32,230
that he's heard from outside through the suttas and

91
00:04:32,230 --> 00:04:32,630
right teaching.

92
00:04:32,630 --> 00:04:34,300
when mind stops

93
00:04:34,300 --> 00:04:34,840
doing that,

94
00:04:34,840 --> 00:04:37,510
with the previous knowledge of what craving is,

95
00:04:37,510 --> 00:04:39,300
to be able to see, ''ah this is the absence of craving''

96
00:04:39,300 --> 00:04:42,820
and he will be able to see right there, ''ah there is no suffering''

97
00:04:42,820 --> 00:04:48,200
And then you'll be also able to understand what that

98
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:50,820
suffering was, even the suffering of the past.

99
00:04:50,820 --> 00:04:53,530
Before he understood the way out,

100
00:04:53,530 --> 00:04:56,410
he wouldn't be suffering on account of that either.

101
00:04:56,410 --> 00:04:57,800
The same knowledge would be applied to

102
00:04:57,800 --> 00:05:00,770
the present, past and future.

103
00:05:10,770 --> 00:05:16,220
Q: How to endure those

104
00:05:16,220 --> 00:05:17,850
painful feelings

105
00:05:17,850 --> 00:05:22,200
you have them now?

106
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:23,010
A: You endure them

107
00:05:23,010 --> 00:05:25,340
basically, instead of enduring,

108
00:05:25,340 --> 00:05:27,860
you want to give in to sensuality

109
00:05:27,860 --> 00:05:30,210
or you want to give in to ill-will or distraction.

110
00:05:30,210 --> 00:05:31,430
Well, you don't do that.

111
00:05:31,430 --> 00:05:33,890
Then, that would result in you having to endure them

112
00:05:33,890 --> 00:05:36,080
but sometimes if you can,

113
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:38,870
you don't have to endure them

114
00:05:38,870 --> 00:05:41,560
without having to give in to sensuality, aversion

115
00:05:41,560 --> 00:05:42,490
or delusion

116
00:05:42,490 --> 00:05:43,760
then, that's fine as well.

117
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:45,430
So you don't have to just constantly going

118
00:05:45,430 --> 00:05:46,650
looking for pain, to endure

119
00:05:46,650 --> 00:05:50,820
that wouldn't necessarily result in wisdom.

120
00:06:01,810 --> 00:06:04,600
Q: Then how does one know if you're free

121
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:05,390
from craving?

122
00:06:06,270 --> 00:06:12,720
A: Because there's no suffering amidst suffering. There is no suffering because you CANNOT suffer.

123
00:06:12,720 --> 00:06:14,320
Not because you're hiding away from it

124
00:06:14,320 --> 00:06:16,360
or because you're not

125
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:20,080
just avoiding things that used to

126
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:22,180
cause you to suffer, No.

127
00:06:22,180 --> 00:06:25,120
Because avoiding things means you're afraid of something already.

128
00:06:25,120 --> 00:06:28,030
A person doesn't leave

129
00:06:28,030 --> 00:06:28,650
a kuti

130
00:06:28,650 --> 00:06:29,860
then, they don't have to talk to anyone

131
00:06:29,860 --> 00:06:32,240
because it might annoy them and then suffer.

132
00:06:32,240 --> 00:06:34,000
So they aren't free from suffering,

133
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:36,660
they're just protecting their precarious environment

134
00:06:36,660 --> 00:06:38,680
of non-disturbance.

135
00:06:38,680 --> 00:06:40,050
But the fact that you must protect it,

136
00:06:40,050 --> 00:06:42,120
means you're disturbed by that,

137
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:48,070
which means they're not truly Not suffering, they're just hiding away from the greater extent of it

138
00:06:48,070 --> 00:06:48,720
So you want to recognize it.

139
00:06:48,720 --> 00:06:48,980
That's why

140
00:06:48,980 --> 00:06:54,200
Conscientious man doesn't neglect his duty, certain things that you must do,

141
00:06:54,200 --> 00:06:56,450
they're not necessarily connected,

142
00:06:56,450 --> 00:06:59,420
just sitting in solitude and practising

143
00:06:59,420 --> 00:07:02,960
like here, we live by ourselves, we do things ourselves

144
00:07:02,960 --> 00:07:06,280
so we have to go and fix the water line.

145
00:07:07,430 --> 00:07:08,540
I don't have to,

146
00:07:08,540 --> 00:07:12,930
but then I won't have any water.

147
00:07:12,930 --> 00:07:14,570
But having to do that, doesn't bother you either.

148
00:07:14,570 --> 00:07:18,200
You're not seeking out as a distraction,

149
00:07:18,200 --> 00:07:19,390
but you're not running away from it

150
00:07:19,390 --> 00:07:20,570
when it arises on its own

151
00:07:20,570 --> 00:07:21,190
as something that's

152
00:07:21,190 --> 00:07:28,180
necessary to be done to sustain the way you live in.

153
00:07:28,180 --> 00:07:30,650
So you need to have again, that self-honesty,

154
00:07:30,650 --> 00:07:31,080
So you know,

155
00:07:31,080 --> 00:07:32,070
you're not hiding away.

156
00:07:32,070 --> 00:07:32,940
You're not indulging,

157
00:07:32,940 --> 00:07:35,650
you're not covering anything up, with that

158
00:07:35,650 --> 00:07:36,210
self-honesty,

159
00:07:36,210 --> 00:07:37,390
and restraint

160
00:07:37,390 --> 00:07:38,830
of the senses, seeing the danger in slightest fault,

161
00:07:38,830 --> 00:07:41,330
moderation in eating,

162
00:07:41,330 --> 00:07:41,890
they'll result in

163
00:07:41,890 --> 00:07:44,830
just obviously being mindful of your actions.

164
00:07:44,830 --> 00:07:48,840
You start discerning mental Intentions, by discerning them

165
00:07:48,980 --> 00:07:52,160
basically, mind is already developing certain perspective

166
00:07:52,160 --> 00:07:56,000
because there is no craving without intention.

167
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,330
But there is intention without craving.

168
00:07:58,330 --> 00:08:00,810
That's why Arahant still can intend and decide

169
00:08:00,810 --> 00:08:01,810
and choose

170
00:08:01,810 --> 00:08:04,200
but he has no craving.

171
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:07,700
But in order to see that, you have to see the intentions

172
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:08,540
to begin with,

173
00:08:08,540 --> 00:08:11,610
most people are not even aware of the mental intentions.

174
00:08:11,610 --> 00:08:14,690
They think intention is just the most obvious choice,

175
00:08:14,690 --> 00:08:15,290
but it's not,

176
00:08:15,290 --> 00:08:17,630
it's just little inclinations, thoughts in themselves

177
00:08:17,630 --> 00:08:21,150
are already intentional.

178
00:08:21,150 --> 00:08:23,630
So it's subtler, and in order to reach the subtler level,

179
00:08:23,630 --> 00:08:27,370
this whole sense restraint, restrained by Patimokkha

180
00:08:27,370 --> 00:08:29,440
by virtue, moderation

181
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:36,460
in eating, mindfulness, is absolutely necessary, not negotiable. And with right instructions, and right way of

182
00:08:36,460 --> 00:08:37,650
looking, that's where the practice is.

183
00:08:37,650 --> 00:08:40,170
Without the right instruction,

184
00:08:40,170 --> 00:08:42,310
it is just restraint, which is good,

185
00:08:42,310 --> 00:08:47,110
but it doesn't lead you to any knowledge, but with the right instruction and that, that's all

186
00:08:47,110 --> 00:08:49,210
you need.

187
00:08:49,210 --> 00:08:50,540
Because sometimes people might think,

188
00:08:50,540 --> 00:08:53,650
OK, restraint is not the Dhamma, that's true

189
00:08:53,650 --> 00:08:55,840
and then they'd think, ''Ok now, I got the Dhamma

190
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:57,210
so I don't have to restrain'', No.

191
00:08:57,210 --> 00:09:02,070
Dhamma applies only where the restraint is.

192
00:09:02,070 --> 00:09:03,520
So, you can see.

193
00:09:03,520 --> 00:09:06,020
Yes, Restraint is not the Dhamma, as in the application of

194
00:09:06,020 --> 00:09:09,540
dhamma, is not the same as the necessary basis

195
00:09:09,540 --> 00:09:09,880
for the

196
00:09:09,880 --> 00:09:10,820
application,

197
00:09:10,820 --> 00:09:11,700
but you wouldn't be able to apply it

198
00:09:11,700 --> 00:09:17,990
if there is no necessary basis.

199
00:09:17,990 --> 00:09:20,510
And if the mind practises like that,

200
00:09:20,510 --> 00:09:24,240
then, the inclination

201
00:09:24,240 --> 00:09:27,220
in form of craving, is becoming more and more obvious.

202
00:09:27,220 --> 00:09:31,640
Why? Because you start recognizing that certain ways

203
00:09:31,640 --> 00:09:33,380
when you intend and incline,

204
00:09:33,380 --> 00:09:38,190
makes you suffer, makes you feel too much, so to speak.

205
00:09:38,190 --> 00:09:42,000
Makes you too involved, exposes you,

206
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:44,000
makes you liable,

207
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,450
by discerning those things, you stop intending like that.

208
00:09:51,300 --> 00:09:52,980
By not intending like that, you're not perpetuating

209
00:09:52,980 --> 00:09:57,510
the craving.

210
00:10:04,190 --> 00:10:10,300
Q: In terms of feelings?

211
00:10:10,300 --> 00:10:14,370
A: Yes, of course, it's always in relation to feelings.

212
00:10:19,370 --> 00:10:24,360
So in an agreeable feeling, that

213
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:26,250
is present,

214
00:10:26,250 --> 00:10:29,570
you have to

215
00:10:29,570 --> 00:10:34,360
discern the inclination

216
00:10:34,360 --> 00:10:35,470
towards wanting more of it

217
00:10:35,470 --> 00:10:36,870
or towards wanting to stay longer,

218
00:10:36,870 --> 00:10:39,530
towards wanting to not go away soon,

219
00:10:39,530 --> 00:10:40,900
towards wanting to increase it,

220
00:10:40,900 --> 00:10:43,140
to intensify it, to prolong it,

221
00:10:43,140 --> 00:10:48,300
any of those things. In a disagreeable feeling,

222
00:10:48,300 --> 00:10:50,380
be the general disagreeable mood or something

223
00:10:50,380 --> 00:10:51,780
more specific,

224
00:10:51,780 --> 00:10:53,380
you have to remove (the inclination)

225
00:10:53,380 --> 00:10:55,350
or rather discern, and by discerning you

226
00:10:55,350 --> 00:10:59,740
remove it automatically, inclination towards resisting it.

227
00:10:59,740 --> 00:11:02,020
Towards trying to find the justification for it.

228
00:11:02,020 --> 00:11:04,390
Towards trying to find an explanation for it,

229
00:11:04,390 --> 00:11:06,130
towards psychologizing it.

230
00:11:06,130 --> 00:11:06,920
just any of those

231
00:11:06,920 --> 00:11:08,110
things are mechanism

232
00:11:08,110 --> 00:11:12,100
which you're trying to engage in, so to remove it, get rid of it.

233
00:11:12,100 --> 00:11:16,820
And the subtlest of them is neutral feeling

234
00:11:16,820 --> 00:11:19,050
when it's neither pleasant nor unpleasant.

235
00:11:19,050 --> 00:11:21,340
And that's when people give into distraction, delusion,

236
00:11:21,340 --> 00:11:24,160
indolence, laziness,

237
00:11:24,160 --> 00:11:26,470
mental heedlessness.

238
00:11:26,470 --> 00:11:33,670
So if you don't do any of those 3 things,

239
00:11:33,670 --> 00:11:35,390
you're not perpetuating craving.

240
00:11:35,390 --> 00:11:40,950
Q: And at the same time

241
00:11:40,950 --> 00:11:44,610
you could be able to

242
00:11:44,610 --> 00:11:47,010
feel, to be aware of your feelings.

243
00:11:47,010 --> 00:11:52,540
A: Yes, of course, to the extent they have arisen on their own.

244
00:11:52,540 --> 00:11:56,000
because feelings arise, having arisen, they cease on their own,

245
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:56,380
you have no

246
00:11:56,380 --> 00:12:00,690
say in that.

247
00:12:00,690 --> 00:12:01,480
That's what mindfulness of feeling is,

248
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:06,590
discerning the nature, basically.

249
00:12:06,590 --> 00:12:08,200
Knowing that they have arisen on their own

250
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:12,550
this pleasant experience at the moment, arisen on its own basically.

251
00:12:12,550 --> 00:12:13,670
That's fine.

252
00:12:13,670 --> 00:12:21,080
You try to get rid of it because pleasure is craving? No, it doesn't. Leaning too much

253
00:12:21,080 --> 00:12:21,440
towards that pleasure,

254
00:12:21,440 --> 00:12:23,470
means craving,

255
00:12:23,470 --> 00:12:28,480
leaning away from the disagreeable, means craving.

256
00:12:28,480 --> 00:12:29,930
Leaning towards forgetfulness

257
00:12:29,930 --> 00:12:34,820
and distraction

258
00:12:36,130 --> 00:12:45,980
means craving, in the neutral feeling.

259
00:12:45,980 --> 00:12:50,840
Q: So being aware of those leanings towards feelings is the way?

260
00:12:50,840 --> 00:12:54,220
A: Yes, that's a good way to start.

261
00:12:54,220 --> 00:12:57,080
You can't be having, ''oh this is my craving''

262
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:58,820
Craving is in your attitude,

263
00:12:58,820 --> 00:13:01,210
but you can bring it down so precisely

264
00:13:01,210 --> 00:13:02,860
whereby you'd see either

265
00:13:02,860 --> 00:13:05,960
the presence of suffering or the presence of

266
00:13:05,960 --> 00:13:07,960
the possibility to suffer.

267
00:13:07,960 --> 00:13:09,890
Any of those is generated by the

268
00:13:09,890 --> 00:13:10,540
amount of your leaning

269
00:13:10,540 --> 00:13:13,790
You're automatically generating

270
00:13:13,790 --> 00:13:15,810
possible liability to suffering,

271
00:13:15,810 --> 00:13:19,970
which is in itself, dukka.

272
00:13:19,970 --> 00:13:24,690
So you use that, to know whether you lean or not

273
00:13:24,690 --> 00:13:27,210
Recognition of how liable to suffering

274
00:13:27,210 --> 00:13:27,940
does this make you.

275
00:13:44,550 --> 00:13:49,640
Q: There is no method that can show you that.

276
00:13:49,640 --> 00:13:53,880
A: Of course not. Because method is on the level of

277
00:13:53,880 --> 00:13:56,140
almost like bodily action or certainly

278
00:13:56,140 --> 00:13:57,110
bodily perceptions that

279
00:13:57,110 --> 00:13:59,070
you're perceiving or going through

280
00:13:59,070 --> 00:14:04,550
some motions. We're talking about intentions behind your actions.

281
00:14:04,550 --> 00:14:05,290
So whatever the method you do

282
00:14:05,290 --> 00:14:07,530
you have to look at intention behind, which means method becomes redundant

283
00:14:08,380 --> 00:14:10,920
which means method is your Sila.

284
00:14:10,920 --> 00:14:12,610
Method is your sense restraint,

285
00:14:12,610 --> 00:14:15,870
that is closest method as you can get.

286
00:14:15,870 --> 00:14:17,570
Method is your moderation in eating.

287
00:14:38,690 --> 00:14:45,550
Q: There's no point in

288
00:14:45,550 --> 00:14:49,660
noting every movement of your mind, quickly write it down?

289
00:14:49,660 --> 00:14:54,780
A: It's completely misplaced, looking in the wrong place.

290
00:14:54,780 --> 00:14:55,250
Because you're not seeing

291
00:14:55,250 --> 00:14:57,380
your intention to note.

292
00:14:57,380 --> 00:15:00,530
You couldn't be noting your intention to note.

293
00:15:00,530 --> 00:15:02,800
Noting is an action which is already intended

294
00:15:02,800 --> 00:15:06,680
which is already leaned towards,

295
00:15:06,680 --> 00:15:08,720
and you're not seeing that.

296
00:15:08,720 --> 00:15:09,680
By not seeing that, no amount

297
00:15:09,680 --> 00:15:14,210
of engaging in that action reveals its nature, otherwise Buddha

298
00:15:14,210 --> 00:15:19,370
would have given the method and described in the suttas, when they did ask him what was the direct method,

299
00:15:19,370 --> 00:15:22,660
he said, ''a young man, develops faith, leaves

300
00:15:22,660 --> 00:15:23,390
his home, lives

301
00:15:23,390 --> 00:15:26,300
restrained by the rules of Patimokkha, practises

302
00:15:26,300 --> 00:15:27,140
sense restraint,

303
00:15:27,140 --> 00:15:28,960
sees the danger in the slightest fault

304
00:15:28,960 --> 00:15:29,900
moderation in eating,

305
00:15:29,900 --> 00:15:33,440
and devotes his time basically to wakefulness.

306
00:15:33,440 --> 00:15:41,640
First Watch of the night, 2nd watch of the night, 3rd watch of the night. then he understands rebirth has been destroyed.

307
00:15:41,640 --> 00:15:42,990
And I remember first time I read as a layman,

308
00:15:42,990 --> 00:15:45,120
I was also looking for a method, and I thought this was too general,

309
00:15:45,120 --> 00:15:45,720
why wouldn't he give you

310
00:15:45,720 --> 00:15:53,180
a particular recipe, how to become enlightened? Because there isn't any. This is the most particular

311
00:15:53,180 --> 00:15:55,780
you can get, if you are not seeing it in a direct matter

312
00:15:55,780 --> 00:15:58,340
just because of all the wrong views that are on top of it.

313
00:15:58,340 --> 00:16:00,710
So you need to meet that Buddha's instruction

314
00:16:00,710 --> 00:16:04,160
halfway basically, or even two-thirds of the way to

315
00:16:04,160 --> 00:16:06,270
start to make sense.

316
00:16:06,270 --> 00:16:07,840
but if a person don't change any of you

317
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:18,760
and then they just add on top of their views, their notion of their practices, that's what you can get. Methods and modern Vipassana technique,

318
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:21,870
or methods of concentration and so on

319
00:16:21,870 --> 00:16:23,940
No, you have to look at intention behind action

320
00:16:23,940 --> 00:16:25,600
so you can't concentrate on that,

321
00:16:25,600 --> 00:16:28,270
because it's behind your concentration.

322
00:16:28,270 --> 00:16:30,750
You can discern it, you can know it.

323
00:16:30,750 --> 00:16:31,330
That's why it says

324
00:16:31,330 --> 00:16:35,620
the consciousness is to be fully understood.

325
00:16:35,620 --> 00:16:36,770
Not concentrated on.

326
00:16:41,770 --> 00:16:45,320
Q: So you can't be aware of your Intentions?

327
00:16:45,320 --> 00:16:51,490
A: You can be aware, in that peripheral background manner, but awareness and concentration in terms of techniques

328
00:16:51,490 --> 00:16:53,410
is not the same thing.

329
00:16:53,410 --> 00:16:54,240
People are not aware

330
00:16:54,240 --> 00:16:57,980
when they do meditation techniques, quite opposite, they're practising some sort of

331
00:16:57,980 --> 00:17:00,310
focusing exercises on one thing or the other,

332
00:17:00,310 --> 00:17:15,030
which means there's no general awareness there.
Q: To be able to see your intentions?

333
00:17:15,030 --> 00:17:20,150
A: They can only be seen indirectly.

334
00:17:20,150 --> 00:17:23,020
Q: By the way you are,

335
00:17:23,020 --> 00:17:24,460
whatever you're choosing,

336
00:17:24,460 --> 00:17:25,550
A: They can only be seen indirectly

337
00:17:25,550 --> 00:17:31,940
on the basis of sense restraint and sila.

338
00:17:31,940 --> 00:17:36,540
You can't see them indirectly if you are unrestrained.

339
00:17:40,480 --> 00:17:44,580
Q: If you are not restrained by keeping sila?

340
00:17:50,780 --> 00:17:53,530
A: You can have a notion of it, to some extent

341
00:17:53,530 --> 00:17:57,630
but understanding the Nature, having that clarity

342
00:17:57,630 --> 00:17:59,550
generated to the point of being able to

343
00:17:59,550 --> 00:18:00,670
fully discern it,

344
00:18:00,670 --> 00:18:02,220
you won't have that.

345
00:18:02,220 --> 00:18:04,920
It is just like trying to collect the water

346
00:18:06,080 --> 00:18:08,800
in 10 meter deep pool, tank

347
00:18:08,800 --> 00:18:11,490
we just constantly punching hole in the bottom of it.

348
00:18:11,490 --> 00:18:15,400
So it'll never fill up to the top.

349
00:18:15,400 --> 00:18:16,090
And you need to have

350
00:18:16,090 --> 00:18:17,780
it filled up

351
00:18:17,780 --> 00:18:22,550
basically.

